Avoid pod preparation when reattaching Claude

Use the daemon's prepared connection to open the Claude terminal
directly, so detach and reattach avoid synchronous container checks and
setup RPCs. Only reuse connections whose pod setup and Claude
configuration completed, and keep the original workspace when host
devcontainer files change.

Retain normal preparation for missing or stopped pods and failed cached
connections. Bound terminal handshakes so a stale proxy cannot prevent
recovery. Cover screen replay, fresh sessions, lifecycle changes, and
failed or stalled handshakes with integration tests.
